~~49. index.html Slideshow arrows don't work (neither mobile nor desktop). Also make them start from a random album (not alphabetically) and also appear randomly, not sequentially.~~
    Root cause: the auto-scroll's setInterval only paused on hover/touch of #album-grid, but the
    arrow buttons sit outside that box (siblings, absolutely positioned at negative offsets), so
    hovering/tapping an arrow never paused it -- the continuous scrollLeft+=1 every 16ms kept
    cancelling the arrow's scrollBy({behavior:'smooth'}) animation. Moved those listeners to the
    new #slider-wrap (parent of both). Also replaced scrollBy's native smooth behavior with a
    hand-rolled requestAnimationFrame easing, since native smooth-scroll support is inconsistent
    across mobile browsers/WebViews. Cards are now shuffled into the DOM on each load (build_pages.py
    INDEX_TEMPLATE), so the slider starts from a random album each visit. Couldn't get a live pixel
    verification of the animation itself in this session's browser tool (that tab reports
    document.hidden=true, which fully suspends requestAnimationFrame -- a testing-environment
    artifact); the pause-on-hover fix and shuffle were verified directly.
